\description{
Beyond \code{x} and \code{y}, mixtime vectors can also be mapped to \code{colour},
\code{fill}, \code{alpha}, \code{size}, and \code{linewidth} (e.g. to shade points or lines by
when they occurred). These are the default scales used for mixtime vectors
mapped to those aesthetics, and are automatically applied. To override the
scale's behaviour manually, use \verb{scale_*_mixtime}.
}
